o for the Fukuoka dog you hear a lot of \"~to\" and \"~to yo\" at the end of sentences; for the Aichi dog it's \"~dagane,\" and for Ehime, \"~zonamoshi,\" etc.\n\n(Source: AsianBeat.com, edited)"},"tags":[{"name":"Kids","rank":20,"spoiler":false}],"titles":{"display":"47 Todoufuken","english":null,"native":"47都道府犬","romaji":"47 Todoufuken","synonyms":[]},"trailer":null,"visibility":"general"}